## Why This Is Asked
Tests classic DP with an additional dimension (at most k intervals) and reconstruction—a common pattern in scheduling optimization problems.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a cardinality constraint (at most k intervals)
- Predecessor p(i) computed via binary search on sorted end times
- DP table with an extra dimension tracking the number of selected intervals
- Backtracking reconstruction to output the chosen jobs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueKJobs(jobs, k) {
  const sorted = jobs.map((j, idx) => ({ ...j, idx })).sort((a, b) => a.end - b.end);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const ends = sorted.map(j => j.end);

  const p = (i) => {
    let lo = 0, hi = i - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
      if (ends[mid] <= sorted[i].start) lo = mid + 1;
      else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return hi;
  };

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const prev = p(i - 1) + 1;
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], dp[prev][t - 1] + sorted[i - 1].value);
    }
  }

  const selected = [];
  let t = k;
  for (let i = n; i > 0 && t > 0; i--) {
    if (dp[i][t] !== dp[i - 1][t]) {
      selected.push(sorted[i - 1]);
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], jobs: selected.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with interval constraints and reconstruction using palindromic substrings.

## Key Concepts
- Palindromic substring precomputation in O(n^2)
- DP over prefix length and exact count: dp[i][t]
- Transition considers ending a palindrome at i with start p
- Reconstruction requires backpointers to recover substrings

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPalSubstr(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const isPal = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; --i) {
    for (let j = i; j < n; ++j) {
      if (s[i] === s[j] && (j - i < 2 || isPal[i+1][j-1])) isPal[i][j] = true;
    }
  }
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if (t > 0) {
        for (let p = 0; p < i; p++) {
          if (isPal[p][i-1]) {
            const val = dp[p][t-1] + (i - p);
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction would trace par[] to extract substrings
}
```

